  },
  data: {
    LLM: "1. Deal: 4-3-3 (widow)-4 to each of three players; widow stays face-down. 2. Bidding: Player to dealer's left bids first, then second; if both bid they alternate until one passes; then third player may bid. Bidding continues until one player remains. Six bids from lowest: Solo, Heart Solo, Misère, Guarantee Solo, Spread Misère, Call Solo. 3. Play: Declarer leads (except Spread Misère, where player to declarer's left leads and declarer's hand is spread face-up). Follow suit if possible; if not, play trump if able; no requirement to beat. Winner of trick leads next. 4. Scoring: Card points in tricks (and widow for declarer) determine success; each bid has a fixed score (30–150) paid to or by declarer.",
    Player: "1. Deal: 4-3-3 (widow)-4 to each of three players; widow stays face-down. 2. Bidding: Player to dealer's left bids first, then second; if both bid they alternate until one passes; then third player may bid. Bidding continues until one player remains. Six bids from lowest: Solo, Heart Solo, Misère, Guarantee Solo, Spread Misère, Call Solo. 3. Play: Declarer leads (except Spread Misère, where player to declarer's left leads and declarer's hand is spread face-up). Follow suit if possible; if not, play trump if able; no requirement to beat. Winner of trick leads next. 4. Scoring: Card points in tricks (and widow for declarer) determine success; each bid has a fixed score (30–150) paid to or by declarer.",
    objective: 'As declarer, meet your bid contract (e.g. take at least 61 card points in Solo, avoid all points in Misère, or take all 120 in Call Solo). As defenders, prevent the declarer from making the contract.',
    gameplay: "1. Deal: 4-3-3 (widow)-4 to each of three players; widow stays face-down. 2. Bidding: Player to dealer's left bids first, then second; if both bid they alternate until one passes; then third player may bid. Bidding continues until one player remains. Six bids from lowest: Solo, Heart Solo, Misère, Guarantee Solo, Spread Misère, Call Solo. 3. Play: Declarer leads (except Spread Misère, where player to declarer's left leads and declarer's hand is spread face-up). Follow suit if possible; if not, play trump if able; no requirement to beat. Winner of trick leads next. 4. Scoring: Card points in tricks (and widow for declarer) determine success; each bid has a fixed score (30–150) paid to or by declarer.",
    keyRules: [
      'Must follow suit if possible; if void, must play trump if able.',
      'Card points: A=11, 10=10, K=4, Q=3, J=2; 9-6=0. Total 120.',
      '61+ points wins for declarer in point bids; Misère = zero points; Guarantee = 74 (hearts) or 80 (other); Call Solo = all 120.',
