    turnFlow: "1. Deal: 4-3-3 (widow)-4 to each of three players; widow stays face-down. 2. Bidding: Player to dealer's left bids first, then second; if both bid they alternate until one passes; then third player may bid. Bidding continues until one player remains. Six bids from lowest: Solo, Heart Solo, Misère, Guarantee Solo, Spread Misère, Call Solo. 3. Play: Declarer leads (except Spread Misère, where player to declarer's left leads and declarer's hand is spread face-up). Follow suit if possible; if not, play trump if able; no requirement to beat. Winner of trick leads next. 4. Scoring: Card points in tricks (and widow for declarer) determine success; each bid has a fixed score (30–150) paid to or by declarer.",
