    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 11 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: As declarer, meet your bid contract (e.g. take at least 61 card points in Solo, avoid all points in Misère, or take all 120 in Call Solo). As defenders, prevent the declarer from making the contract.',
      "Turn-flow example: 1. Deal: 4-3-3 (widow)-4 to each of three players; widow stays face-down. 2. Bidding: Player to dealer's left bids first, then second; if both bid they alternate until one passes; then third player may bid. Bidding continues until one player remains. Six bids from lowest: Solo, Heart Solo, Misère, Guarantee Solo, Spread Misère, Call Solo. 3. Play: Declarer leads (except Spread Misère, where player to declarer's left leads and declarer's hand is spread face-up). Follow suit if possible; if not, play trump if able; no requirement to beat. Winner of trick leads next. 4. Scoring: Card points in tricks (and widow for declarer) determine success; each bid has a fixed score (30–150) paid to or by declarer.",
      'Scoring example: Card points in tricks (and widow for declarer): A=11, 10=10, K=4, Q=3, J=2; 9-6=0. Total 120. Declarer must meet contract: Solo/Heart Solo 61+; Guarantee 74 (hearts) or 80 (other); Misère/Spread Misère zero points; Call Solo all 120. Fixed scores per bid (30–150) paid to or by declarer. Declarer wins by meeting the bid contract (e.g. 61+ points in Solo, zero in Misère, all 120 in Call Solo); defenders win by defeating the contract..',
